+To keep this vignette quick to build, we'll run `qap_run` with 100 permutations (`reps = 100`) rather than the default of 500. Fewer permutations means the permutation-based p-values reported below are less precise. They are fine for illustration, but for your own analyses we recommend keeping the default of 500 or using more. As far as variables go in this example, we'll include `same_sex`, `both_race_White`, and `abs_diff_grade`. 
 
 ```{r qap_run}
